{"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Articles","anchor":"Articles","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/IndexConventions","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/SafeInterpolation","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/ConcurrencyModel","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/StoringCustomTypes","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/QueryingJSON","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/TransactionsAndServices"]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/loomcore\/fulltextsearch"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Match, rank, and excerpt text with typed expressions over SQLite’s FTS5 extension."}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Topics","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FTS5Table","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FTS5Query","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/MatchExpression","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/BM25","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Snippet","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Highlight"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FullTextSearch","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"SQLite ships FTS5 — virtual tables with a full-text index, the ","type":"text"},{"code":"MATCH","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" operator, ","type":"text"},{"code":"bm25","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" relevance scoring, and the ","type":"text"},{"code":"snippet","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"highlight","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" auxiliary functions — and every OS version LoomCore supports includes it. This article shows the typed expression DSL over those features.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Creating the index itself stays plain SQL, in line with LoomCore not being an ORM:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["try await db.exec(raw: \"CREATE VIRTUAL TABLE articles USING fts5(title, body)\")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FTS5Table","type":"reference"},{"text":" then names that table for the DSL. Pass ","type":"text"},{"code":"columns","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (in declaration order) when you plan to use ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FTS5Table\/snippet(column:prefix:suffix:ellipsis:maxTokens:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FTS5Table\/highlight(column:prefix:suffix:)","type":"reference"},{"text":", which address columns by name; matching and ranking work without it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let articles = FTS5Table(\"articles\", columns: [\"title\", \"body\"])"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Matching","text":"Matching"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FTS5Table\/match(_:)-2fk37","type":"reference"},{"text":" builds the ","type":"text"},{"code":"MATCH","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" predicate. The query string uses FTS5’s own syntax — bare tokens are AND-ed, ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"quoted text\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a phrase, ","type":"text"},{"code":"title : swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" filters a column — and is bound as a parameter, so it can never escape the ","type":"text"},{"code":"MATCH","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" operand into SQL:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let articles = FTS5Table(\"articles\")","let userInput = \"swift database\"","","let hits = try await db.query(","  \"SELECT title FROM articles WHERE \\(articles.match(userInput))\"",") { stmt, _ in","  try String.column(of: stmt, at: 0)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Binding is the opposite choice from ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/JSONPath","type":"reference"},{"text":", which inlines its paths so SQLite can match expression indexes; no such optimization applies to ","type":"text"},{"code":"MATCH","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and binding means statements differing only in search text share one prepared-statement cache entry. The cost of accepting raw syntax is that a malformed query — an unclosed quote, a dangling ","type":"text"},{"code":"AND","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — only fails when SQLite executes the statement, surfacing as a thrown ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/LoomError","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Binding prevents SQL injection; it does not sandbox the FTS5 query language itself. A whole-table match hands the searcher FTS5’s full grammar, including column filters over ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"every","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" indexed column — ","type":"text"},{"code":"secret : guess","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" probes a column your UI never displays, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" prefixes narrow guesses further. Pass raw user input through only when every indexed column is meant to be user-searchable. Otherwise route user text through ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FTS5Query\/phrase(_:fromStart:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FTS5Query\/prefix(_:fromStart:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (metacharacters are inert there), scope the search with an explicit ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FTS5Query\/column(_:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" filter or a single-column ","type":"text"},{"code":"match(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (an inner filter cannot widen a column-scoped match), and keep text that must never be searchable out of the FTS5 index entirely.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside","name":"Important"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A single column can be matched directly through ","type":"text"},{"code":"match(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on a ","type":"text"},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"-typed ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/ColumnExpression","type":"reference"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let title = ColumnExpression<String>(\"title\")","let titled = try await db.query(\"SELECT title FROM articles WHERE \\(title.match(\"swift\"))\") { stmt, _ in","  try String.column(of: stmt, at: 0)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A match predicate composes with ","type":"text"},{"code":"&&","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" only. It also type-checks under ","type":"text"},{"code":"||","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and prefix ","type":"text"},{"code":"!","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", but SQLite rejects ","type":"text"},{"code":"MATCH","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in those positions at execution — express alternatives and exclusions inside the query itself with ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FTS5Query\/or(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FTS5Query\/not(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"The-query-builder","text":"The query builder"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For queries assembled in code, ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FTS5Query","type":"reference"},{"text":" renders FTS5 syntax that is correct by construction. Phrase text is always quoted with embedded quotes doubled, so it is treated as data — ","type":"text"},{"code":"*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"^","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":":","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and operators inside it have no effect:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let articles = FTS5Table(\"articles\")","","\/\/ (\"swift concurrency\" AND \"actor\"*) — a phrase requires adjacent tokens,","\/\/ a prefix matches \"actor\", \"actors\", \"actor-isolated\", …","let query = FTS5Query.phrase(\"swift concurrency\").and(.prefix(\"actor\"))","","let hits = try await db.query(","  \"SELECT title FROM articles WHERE \\(articles.match(query))\"",") { stmt, _ in","  try String.column(of: stmt, at: 0)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FTS5Query\/phrase(_:fromStart:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FTS5Query\/prefix(_:fromStart:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" are the leaves (","type":"text"},{"code":"fromStart","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" prepends ","type":"text"},{"code":"^","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", matching only at the start of a column); ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FTS5Query\/and(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FTS5Query\/or(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FTS5Query\/not(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" combine them, always parenthesizing so precedence never depends on FTS5’s grammar. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FTS5Query\/near(_:distance:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" requires phrases to appear close together, and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FTS5Query\/column(_:_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FTS5Query\/columns(_:_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" restrict a sub-query to specific columns:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/\/ {\"title\" \"summary\"} : (NEAR(\"swift\" \"database\", 5) OR \"sqlite\")","let query = FTS5Query.columns(","  [\"title\", \"summary\"],","  .near([\"swift\", \"database\"], distance: 5).or(.phrase(\"sqlite\"))",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The rendered query is bound exactly like a raw string, so the two entry points mix freely.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Ranking","text":"Ranking"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Within a full-text query, the hidden ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FTS5Table\/rank","type":"reference"},{"text":" column carries each row’s relevance score. Scores are negative and lower is more relevant, so ascending ","type":"text"},{"code":"ORDER BY","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" returns the best matches first:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let articles = FTS5Table(\"articles\")","let best = try await db.query(","  \"SELECT title FROM articles WHERE \\(articles.match(\"swift\")) ORDER BY \\(articles.rank)\"",") { stmt, _ in","  try String.column(of: stmt, at: 0)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Outside a ","type":"text"},{"code":"MATCH","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" statement the column is NULL, hence its ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double?","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FTS5Table\/bm25(weights:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" exposes the same scoring function with per-column weights — one weight per indexed column, in declaration order:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let articles = FTS5Table(\"articles\", columns: [\"title\", \"body\"])","","\/\/ Matches in the title count ten times as much as matches in the body.","let ranked = try await db.query(","  \"SELECT title FROM articles WHERE \\(articles.match(\"swift\")) ORDER BY \\(articles.bm25(weights: [10, 1]))\"",") { stmt, _ in","  try String.column(of: stmt, at: 0)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Snippets-and-highlights","text":"Snippets and highlights"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FTS5Table\/snippet(column:prefix:suffix:ellipsis:maxTokens:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" extracts a fragment of matched text — up to ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxTokens","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" tokens (at most 64) around the best match, with each matched token wrapped in ","type":"text"},{"code":"prefix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"suffix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and truncation marked by ","type":"text"},{"code":"ellipsis","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FTS5Table\/highlight(column:prefix:suffix:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" returns the column’s full text with the same marking:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let articles = FTS5Table(\"articles\", columns: [\"title\", \"body\"])","","let results = try await db.query(","  \"\"\"","  SELECT","    \\(articles.highlight(column: \"title\", prefix: \"<b>\", suffix: \"<\/b>\")),","    \\(articles.snippet(column: \"body\", prefix: \"<b>\", suffix: \"<\/b>\", ellipsis: \"…\", maxTokens: 12))","  FROM articles WHERE \\(articles.match(\"swift\")) ORDER BY \\(articles.rank)","  \"\"\"",") { stmt, _ in","  (try String?.column(of: stmt, at: 0), try String?.column(of: stmt, at: 1))","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"SQLite identifies these columns by positional index; LoomCore resolves the name against the table’s declared ","type":"text"},{"code":"columns","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so the list must include every column you excerpt. Both functions return NULL — hence ","type":"text"},{"code":"String?","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — when the underlying column value is NULL. Omitting ","type":"text"},{"code":"column:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from ","type":"text"},{"code":"snippet","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lets FTS5 pick the most relevant column itself.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"warning","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The declared "},{"code":"columns","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order is load-bearing and never checked against the live table. If a migration reorders or inserts a column and the Swift declaration isn’t updated, the name resolves to a valid but ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"wrong","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" index and every snippet and highlight silently excerpts the wrong column — no error is raised. Pin the declaration to the live schema with "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FTS5Table\/verifyColumns(on:)"},{"type":"text","text":" in an integration test or at startup."}]}],"type":"aside","name":"Warning"}]}],"metadata":{"role":"collectionGroup","roleHeading":"API Collection","title":"Full-Text Search","modules":[{"name":"LoomCore"}]},"kind":"article","sections":[],"references":{"doc://LoomCore/docum